WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.503 --> 00:00:02.503
- Excuse me, could I ask you a question?

00:00:03.574 --> 00:00:07.276
(pocket translator speaking
in foreign language)

00:00:07.276 --> 00:00:08.693
- I think this is the
weirdest conversation

00:00:08.693 --> 00:00:10.373
you and I have ever had.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.610
- [Narrator] This is Barcelona

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.100
and this is Alex Rawlings, he's a.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.220
- I am a journalist, a writer

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.726
and a filmmaker and a polyglot.

00:00:20.726 --> 00:00:22.310
(soft music)

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.447
- [Narrator] He's also the author of

00:00:23.447 --> 00:00:25.600
"How to speak any language fluently".

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.240
- I spent my whole life telling people

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.810
about the benefits of learning languages

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.480
and learning languages myself.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.580
- [Narrator] So a better
person to help us test this.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.380
- A brand new Pocketalk device,
which is a live translator

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.420
which in theory should replace the need

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.020
of learning foreign languages.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.780
to see whether I can communicate

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.754
with people in Barcelona using it.

00:00:43.754 --> 00:00:46.171
(soft music)

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.540
- [Narrator] Why did we
pick this translator?

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.160
A few reasons, with the
click of one button,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.720
it can translate 82 different languages

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.720
and it claims to translate conversations

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.600
not just statements.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.900
- Lets set the languages

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.430
I'm setting the input
language to English, UK

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.190
and the output language to Spanish, Spain.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.697
- [Narrator] It has noise
canceling microphones

00:01:09.697 --> 00:01:12.450
and speakers so speak in one language

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.770
and outcomes another.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.730
- We have a microphone
on this side, a speaker

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:17.920
and a microphone on this side.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.810
So presumably you can
use it like this to talk.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.470
- [Narrator] It's
smaller than a smartphone

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.930
but it still has a touch screen

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.060
and it comes with two
years of cellular data.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.650
So those traveling don't need to worry

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.570
about an international data plan.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.247
- This feels like a very comfortable thing

00:01:31.247 --> 00:01:32.540
to have in my pocket

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:35.220
and very easy to whip
out whenever I need it

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.600
and it's extremely light actually

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.550
I barely feel like I've got
a device in my hand at all.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:41.530
- [Narrator] It also has a camera

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.920
for translating signs and menus.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.213
It costs $299, but is it worth it?

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.720
- So I've designed three tests today

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.933
to see how well the
Pocketalk device performs.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.970
First up, we're going to try

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.294
for a simple, typical tourist interaction.

00:02:00.294 --> 00:02:03.223
Could I have a coffee
with soy milk please?

00:02:04.466 --> 00:02:07.773
(pocketalk speaking in foreign language)

00:02:07.773 --> 00:02:08.998
(waitress speaking in foreign language)

00:02:08.998 --> 00:02:10.310
(Alex speaking in foreign language)

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.032
(waitress speaking in foreign language)

00:02:14.032 --> 00:02:15.880
- [Pocketalk] Right now.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.850
- Okay, so the first direction
seemed to go quite well.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.570
She didn't seem to react weirdly

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.340
for me speaking to her through
a live translation machine

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.550
and when she brought my
coffee, she brought soy milk

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.750
so that passed the test as well.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.167
(soft music)

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.059
Could you tell me the way
to the cathedral please?

00:02:37.059 --> 00:02:40.720
(pocketalk speaking in foreign language)

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.350
(passerby speaking in foreign language)

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.759
- One second.

00:02:44.759 --> 00:02:49.426
(passerby speaking in foreign language)

00:02:52.697 --> 00:02:54.640
- [Pocketalk] Look, you go up Viary Lane

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.510
and when you get to Jaime's height

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.410
you first have your left hand.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:03.310
- Sorry, could you tell me that again?

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.380
I'm not sure, I understood

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.663
what was the way to the cathedral please?

00:03:08.197 --> 00:03:12.947
(pocketalk speaking in foreign language)

00:03:16.966 --> 00:03:17.960
(passerby speaking in foreign language)

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:18.883
- One second.

00:03:20.731 --> 00:03:25.398
(passerby speaking in foreign language)

00:03:33.725 --> 00:03:34.957
- [Pocketalk] You Keep walking

00:03:34.957 --> 00:03:37.503
until you reach the main
street that is Via Laietana

00:03:37.503 --> 00:03:39.800
and you go up and on the left,

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.000
when you get to Jaime
you will first see it.

00:03:43.215 --> 00:03:45.630
- I'm not sure it fully
understood my accent,

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.070
I'm not sure it really
understood the person

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.650
in the streets accent.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.660
At some point, when I asked

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.150
do you know the way to the cathedral?

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.020
I think it thought I said

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.830
do you know the weight of the cathedral?

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:55.910
There are also moments where I think

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:58.220
it took a really long time
to actually translate.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.190
So I'm trying to stop
someone in the street

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:04.310
who's in a rush and luckily
Barcelona is a relaxed city.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.330
So it's not such a big problem

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.434
so I'd say that I'm not sure we can say

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.660
that it passed that test.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.140
Now for the hardest trial

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.560
that I'm gonna put this device through.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.280
This is my friend Ash, he's
a tattoo artist from Egypt

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.650
he's been living here in Barcelona

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.860
and normally when we see
each other we speak English.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.860
But this time he's going to
speak to me in Egyptian, Arabic.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.330
When this device is speaking Arabic

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.750
do you understand it very well?

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.320
What are the things that is translating?

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.733
What is it not translating?

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:38.732
(pocketalk speaking in foreign language)

00:04:41.993 --> 00:04:46.243
(Ash speaking in foreign language)

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.180
- [Pocketalk] It is fine,

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:59.510
it's just necessary to answer
the Arabic language in Egypt

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:02.490
but work within a hospital
with a translator.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:05.163
All words translate correct
words and wrong words.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.450
- I didn't understand
any of the translation

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.760
of what Ash was saying to her.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.820
It was saying all sorts of weird
words, weird constructions.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:15.920
Ash said that it understood
my English very well

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.270
and it was translating my English

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.620
into pretty good standard Arabic.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.260
But the thing with Arabic

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.956
is that everybody speaks
regional languages.

00:05:22.956 --> 00:05:25.440
So that's what the device is claim that

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.480
it is able to pick up and
translate colloquial language

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.700
in a really good way

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:33.503
I've got to say, I'm not
entirely sure that was a success.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.127
- [Narrator] A Pocketalk spokesman said,

00:05:36.127 --> 00:05:38.180
"We are constantly updating our software

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:39.457
to improve performance.

00:05:39.457 --> 00:05:41.860
Translating slang and various dialects

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.780
can be difficult to get
right 100% of the time."

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.770
He added, "The speed of translation

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.730
depends on the strength
of the user signal."

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:51.690
So where did Alex net out?

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:54.760
- I would probably give
this device three stars.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.140
It's a great piece of kit,

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.540
it's a great size, very portable

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.350
and for basic transactions
buying things in shops

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.220
it definitely does what
it's supposed to do.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:05.760
But if you have aspirations of being

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.300
more than just a transactional
person in a foreign country

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.047
I don't think this device
is really gonna cut it.

00:06:11.047 --> 00:06:14.880
(singing in foreign language)

00:06:20.288 --> 00:06:21.121
- No.

